TI  - Whole lung lavage.
PG  - 543-58
AB  - After more than 35 years of evolution, whole lung lavage is an efficient and safe 
      technique. Furthermore, it can be a pleasant experience because it consists of 
      performing general anesthesia without a surgeon being in the operating room. 
      Whole lung lavage can be adapted to many patients and diseases; however, more 
      research must be done to confirm the new indications.
