PG  - 373-382
LID - S0272-5231(25)00016-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2025.02.014 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis is a rare disease characterized by accumulation of 
      lipoproteinaceous material in the distal airspaces. The most common form, 
      autoimmune, is due to autoantibodies against granulocyte macrophage colony 
      stimulating factor (GM-CSF), which impairs macrophage clearance of surfactant 
      from alveolar spaces. Treatment for symptomatic patients includes whole lung 
      lavage and GM-CSF augmentation therapy.
