TI  - Whole Lung Lavage in Autoimmune Pulmonary Alveolar Proteinosis: Unique Challenges 
      in a Resource-Limited Setting.
PG  - e9588
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.9588 [doi]
LID - e9588
AB  - Autoimmune pulmonary alveolar proteinosis (PAP) is characterized by antibodies to 
      granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF), alveolar macrophage 
      dysfunction, and surfactant accumulation. Whole lung lavage (WLL) is the 
      treatment of choice in patients with PAP and severe hypoxemia. In 
      resource-limited settings, WLL can be performed in the intubated, anesthetized 
      patient who is being one lung ventilated using a Y-type bladder irrigation 
      catheter for saline instillation and drainage.
