TI  - Bilateral whole lung lavage in pulmonary alveolar proteinosis--a retrospective 
      study.
PG  - 254-9
LID - S0873-2159(14)00076-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.rppneu.2014.04.004 [doi]
AB  - Whole lung lavage (WLL) is the gold standard technique for the treatment of 
      Pulmonary Alveolar Proteinosis (PAP). In this paper we evaluated and discuss 
      bilateral WLL, namely the procedure work-up and the therapeutic efficacy. Six 
      bilateral WLL performed through a careful adherence to a modified Royal Brompton 
      Hospital (London) technique were carried out without major complications and were 
      associated with clinical and functional improvement of the PAP patients submitted 
      to this procedure. As there are benefits in terms of time, patient comfort and 
      cost effectiveness compared to unilateral WLL, associated with the efficacy and 
      safety observed, bilateral WLL seems to be a suitable first choice for 
      therapeutic lavage in PAP patients.
