VI  - 34
IP  - 6
DP  - 2021
TI  - Power washing pulmonary alveolar proteinosis.
PG  - 731-733
LID - 10.1080/08998280.2021.1953884 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis is an uncommon cause of insidious onset shortness 
      of breath and hypoxemia. It is caused by an accumulation of surfactant within the 
      alveoli. Left untreated, it can be fatal. Standard-of-care treatment is 
      whole-lung lavage; however, in severe cases, the associated hypoxemia can be 
      profound and single-lung ventilation would not be tolerated, potentially 
      preventing a lifesaving treatment. Single cases using veno-venous extracorporeal 
      membrane oxygenation to perform whole-lung lavage have been reported. Here we 
      describe three patients with severe pulmonary alveolar proteinosis who were 
      successfully treated with whole-lung lavage using veno-venous extracorporeal 
      membrane oxygenation for oxygenation support.
