DP  - 2026 Apr 1
TI  - Impact of Saline Instillation and Drainage on Oxygenation During Whole Lung 
      Lavage.
PG  - 294-296
LID - 10.4103/aca.aca_262_25 [doi]
AB  - Whole lung lavage (WLL) for pulmonary alveolar proteinosis, performed under 
      one-lung ventilation (OLV), illustrates the dynamic interplay between alveolar 
      expansion and pulmonary vascular responses. Instillation of warm saline into the 
      nonventilated lung compresses pulmonary vessels, mimicking hypoxic pulmonary 
      vasoconstriction and enhancing oxygenation. Conversely, drainage of the saline 
      relieves vascular compression, worsens ventilation-perfusion (V/Q) mismatch, and 
      leads to a decline in oxygenation. This cyclical pattern underscores the 
      physiological shifts that influence oxygenation during WLL.
