DP  - 2005 Jan
TI  - Whole lung lavage with intermittent double lung ventilation. A modified technique 
      for managing pulmonary alveolar proteinosis.
PG  - 139-41
AB  - Whole lung lavage is still the most effective treatment for pulmonary alveolar 
      proteinosis. We report a 21-year-old male diagnosed with pulmonary alveolar 
      proteinosis by open lung biopsy and who underwent whole lung lavage with a 
      modified technique. He showed significant improvement in clinical and functional 
      parameters. The technique of intermittent double lung ventilation during lavage 
      procedure keeps the oxygen saturation in acceptable limits in patients at risk 
      for severe hypoxemia and allows the procedure to be completed in a single 
      setting.
