TI  - Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis associated with psoriasis and complicated by 
      mycobacterial infection: successful treatment with granulocyte-macrophage colony 
      stimulating factor after a partial response to whole lung lavage.
PG  - 419-22
AB  - Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis (PAP) is a rare lung disease. Although whole lung 
      lavage is considered the most effective treatment, not every patient shows a 
      complete response. The case ofa young man with PAP in association with psoriasis 
      who underwent frequent whole lung lavage but only achieved remission following 
      treatment with granulocyte-macrophage colony stimulating factor (GM-CSF) is 
      reported. His lung problem was complicated by atypical mycobacterial 
      infection,which resolved with treatment. The role of GM-CSF is discussed.
