TI  - [Research progress of cell therapy in hereditary pulmonary alveolar proteinosis].
PG  - 730-734
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.cn112147-20230107-00008 [doi]
AB  - Hereditary pulmonary alveolar proteinosis (hPAP) is a rare interstitial lung 
      disease caused by mutation in CSF2RA/CSF2RB, characterized by the deposition of 
      pulmonary surfactant due to the alveolar macrophage dysfunction. The whole lung 
      lavage can effectively alleviate the symptoms but is associated with potential 
      complications. Cell therapy is a novel approach with advances that provide a new 
      therapeutic strategy for the treatment of hPAP.
