TI  - The combination of inhaled nitric oxide and pulmonary artery balloon inflation 
      improves oxygenation during whole-lung lavage.
PG  - 676-679
LID - 10.1213/01.ANE.0000133243.59867.A1 [doi]
AB  - We present a case in which the use of inhaled nitric oxide associated with 
      temporary partial unilateral pulmonary artery occlusion further improved 
      oxygenation during whole-lung lavage. This is the first case in the literature 
      describing the simultaneous use of these two modalities.
