      sarcoidosis?
PG  - 90-4
AB  - Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis (PAP) is a rare lung disease characterized by the 
      accumulation of surfactant phospholipids and lipoproteins within the alveoli. 
      Here we report on a female patient who was diagnosed with autoimmune PAP and 
      successfully treated with whole lung lavage (WLL). 15 months after PAP diagnosis 
      the patient developed marked fatigue. Additional tests revealed the diagnosis of 
      sarcoidosis. We can only speculate that PAP and sarcoidosis in our patient are 
      linked to each other based on the fact that other autoimmune disorders have also 
      been associated with sarcoidosis.
