PMID- 15770973
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20050628
LR  - 20190922
IS  - 0914-7187 (Print)
IS  - 0914-7187 (Linking)
VI  - 19
IP  - 1
DP  - 2005 Feb
TI  - Mismatch between gallium-67 uptake and CT findings in a case of pulmonary 
      alveolar proteinosis.
PG  - 47-50
AB  - Gallium-67 citrate (67Ga) scintigraphy has been used as an indicator of activity 
      of diffuse interstitial lung diseases. However, little has been mentioned in 
      pulmonary alveolar proteinosis (PAP). Here we present a 53-year-old man with PAP 
      showing patchy 67Ga uptake by single photon emission computed tomography (SPECT). 
      Interestingly, the strong 67Ga uptake was observed in areas where ground-glass 
      opacities were faint on chest CT. The uptake persisted after whole-lung lavage 
      while the ground-glass opacity improved markedly. Although the precise mechanism 
      of 67Ga uptake remains unclear, 67Ga SPECT findings may reflect the different 
      pathological condition of PAP than that shown by CT.
