TI  - [The extracorporeal circulation in the treatment of pulmonary diseases].
PG  - 409-13
AB  - The extracorporeal circulation is seldom used in pulmonary surgery. In this 
      paper, we present some clinical cases and discuss the different indications for 
      extracorporeal circulation in pulmonary diseases. Pulmonary embolectomy and lung 
      transplantation are the main indications for the use of heart-lung-machine. Less 
      frequent indications are oxygen support during whole lung lavage in pulmonary 
      alveolar proteinosis. Lung cancer surgery and other indications for 
      extracorporeal circulation are also discussed.
