DP  - 2001 Jun 5
TI  - [The first successful therapeutic pulmonary lavage in pulmonary alveolar 
      proteinosis in the Czech Republic].
PG  - 406-8
AB  - Whole lung lavage represents a possible therapeutic method in pulmonary alveolar 
      proteinosis which can lead to an improvement of blood oxygenation in the lungs. 
      In the Czech Republic there has been no experience with this method so far. A 
      case of 69-year-old female with idiopathic pulmonary alveolar proteinosis treated 
      with the whole lung lavage sequentionally conducted is reported. The whole lung 
      lavage led to the improvement of dyspnoe and arterial blood gases. Whole lung 
      lavage leads to the improvement of clinical status in patients with pulmonary 
      alveolar proteinosis.
